, syntax form, keyword name, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and useful keyword value one shared, responsive completion contract[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]across the prompt input widget and the xprompt LSP.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]xprompt_directive_completion_parity.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/xprompt_directive_completion_parity.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-rj[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-rj/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Canonical directive completion contract in sase-core[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]directive-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]directive-contract: define the complete directive and argument schema, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]grammar-aware cursor context, value-provider roles, and Python bindings [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in sase-core so frontends no longer maintain divergent hard-coded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalogs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Complete contextual directive support in the xprompt LSP[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]external-editor-lsp[dim] · [dim][/dim]after directive-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]external-editor-lsp: drive LSP names, snippets, keyword names, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]contextual values from the shared contract, extending the existing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cached editor catalog bridge for bead and identity targets without [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]blocking editor requests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold 